Let's go.

25
00:01:13,560 --> 00:01:13,760
Let's go.

26
00:01:13,760 --> 00:01:14,320
Let's go.

27
00:01:14,320 --> 00:01:14,860
Let's go.

28
00:01:15,040 --> 00:01:15,380
Let's go.

29
00:01:15,640 --> 00:01:16,240
Let's go.

30
00:01:16,260 --> 00:01:16,740
Let's go.

31
00:01:16,740 --> 00:01:16,880
Let's go.

32
00:01:17,060 --> 00:01:17,500
Let's go.

33
00:01:17,940 --> 00:01:18,160
Let's go.

34
00:01:18,160 --> 00:01:18,480
Let's go.

35
00:01:18,480 --> 00:01:19,000
Let's go.

36
00:02:49,030 --> 00:03:13,510
It's a Hydra. I've never seen one before.

37
00:03:19,030 --> 00:03:27,030
Zenith! What's she doing in there?

38
00:03:27,030 --> 00:03:32,030
You dumbass! Don't rush in!

39
00:03:32,030 --> 00:03:38,030
Rear-line firing! Silent Fist of the Frost Giant! Icicle break!

40
00:03:38,030 --> 00:03:44,030
Stop cannon!

41
00:03:44,030 --> 00:03:47,030
Did it deflect this?

42
00:04:10,030 --> 00:04:13,030
On your right!

43
00:04:14,030 --> 00:04:21,030
Rapid dark currents gush forth! Flash run!

44
00:04:26,030 --> 00:04:29,030
Earthen pillar!

45
00:04:34,030 --> 00:04:37,030
Does magic not work on this abomination?

46
00:04:37,030 --> 00:04:49,030
That sound... Is it a force field? Disturb magic? I can't tell. But I can't touch it. What should I do? Just keep trying?

47
00:04:49,030 --> 00:05:01,030
Rudy, see that? It's healing. We should retreat!

48
00:05:01,030 --> 00:05:02,030
You're up!

49
00:05:02,030 --> 00:05:03,030
I'm on it!

50
00:05:09,030 --> 00:05:11,030
No you don't! We gotta fall back!

51
00:05:11,030 --> 00:05:16,030
Get off, Geese, you traitor! Like hell, I'm just gonna turn back now!

52
00:05:17,030 --> 00:05:18,030
Rotinash!

53
00:05:27,030 --> 00:05:31,030
Retreat! To the magic circle!

54
00:05:31,030 --> 00:05:45,670
Let this divine power be rich and nourishing.

55
00:05:46,310 --> 00:05:48,890
Offering those whose strength has been lost, the strength tries again.

56
00:05:49,590 --> 00:05:49,870
Healing.

57
00:05:51,470 --> 00:05:52,430
Are you all right?

58
00:05:52,950 --> 00:05:54,610
Oh, it was only a scratch.

59
00:05:57,010 --> 00:05:57,790
Hey, Dad.

60
00:06:01,030 --> 00:06:04,670
That was her. That was Zenith. It had to be.

61
00:06:05,630 --> 00:06:07,450
Come on. Stay calm.

62
00:06:08,690 --> 00:06:12,210
Yeah, I know. Sorry. I'm all right now.

63
00:06:14,550 --> 00:06:18,290
Do you think Mom is still alive in there?

64
00:06:19,770 --> 00:06:20,410
What?

65
00:06:21,810 --> 00:06:24,690
What difference does it make? We're saving her.

66
00:06:27,890 --> 00:06:29,130
No, you're right.

67
00:06:29,670 --> 00:06:31,490
Enough of that. No infighting.

68
00:06:31,890 --> 00:06:33,550
Rudy, you saw her.

69
00:06:33,650 --> 00:06:34,490
That was Zenith.

70
00:06:34,670 --> 00:06:36,430
That is your mother in there, son.

71
00:06:36,650 --> 00:06:38,850
How can you be so goddamn calm?

72
00:06:39,890 --> 00:06:42,210
Loosing my composure isn't going to solve anything.

73
00:06:42,550 --> 00:06:43,910
That is not the point.

74
00:06:44,770 --> 00:06:46,910
Maybe I am a little lukewarm.

75
00:06:46,910 --> 00:06:50,830
But I don't have much of a relationship with Zenith.

76
00:06:51,370 --> 00:06:55,170
At this point, she's less my mother than someone I used to live with.

77
00:06:55,830 --> 00:06:58,210
I haven't seen her in almost ten years.

78
00:06:58,670 --> 00:06:59,330
I was seven.

79
00:07:00,690 --> 00:07:01,530
Let's regroup.

80
00:07:01,910 --> 00:07:03,290
Make sure we're on the same page.

81
00:07:03,630 --> 00:07:04,050
What?

82
00:07:04,370 --> 00:07:06,710
Our magic had zero effect on that Guardian.

83
00:07:07,470 --> 00:07:08,930
It regenerates rapidly.

84
00:07:09,690 --> 00:07:12,870
It broke through Alina Lisa's defense just by brushing up against her.

85
00:07:12,870 --> 00:07:16,530
And then there's Mom, who's trapped inside a crystal.

86
00:07:17,050 --> 00:07:19,370
And frankly speaking, we don't know if she's alive or dead.

87
00:07:21,010 --> 00:07:23,150
Oh, piss off. I already know all of that.

88
00:07:23,350 --> 00:07:26,950
What I'm saying is that's not the attitude to have when we finally found her.

89
00:07:26,970 --> 00:07:27,790
Knock that off!

90
00:07:27,910 --> 00:07:30,070
You can argue with each other when we're back at the end!

91
00:07:32,450 --> 00:07:33,670
Had enough of this shit.

92
00:07:33,670 --> 00:07:37,970
Get that out of your system?

93
00:07:38,210 --> 00:07:39,810
Because we need to talk this out.

94
00:07:48,770 --> 00:07:49,810
Hey, it's okay.

95
00:07:50,190 --> 00:07:51,290
If you say so.

96
00:07:52,290 --> 00:07:54,150
Paul and I have butted heads before.

97
00:07:54,870 --> 00:07:56,770
Things are just a little out of whack right now.

98
00:07:57,270 --> 00:07:58,130
Intentions are high.

99
00:07:58,130 --> 00:08:06,230
Well, as far as Zenith is concerned, she's not trapped in there forever.

100
00:08:06,670 --> 00:08:07,170
You think?

101
00:08:07,830 --> 00:08:08,970
I've heard the same.

102
00:08:09,370 --> 00:08:12,470
I know of one other person who was in a very similar situation.

103
00:08:13,130 --> 00:08:14,830
And she is very much alive.

104
00:08:15,430 --> 00:08:17,650
But we'll have to defeat that Guardian first.

105
00:08:18,190 --> 00:08:20,650
And I haven't the faintest idea of where to begin.

106
00:08:21,270 --> 00:08:21,930
No kidding.

107
00:08:22,310 --> 00:08:23,830
You can tell by looking it's a Hydra.

108
00:08:24,050 --> 00:08:26,310
But I've never heard of one with skills like that before.

109
00:08:26,310 --> 00:08:28,930
And the cursed thing can heal itself, too.

110
00:08:29,550 --> 00:08:31,530
It's most likely a manatite Hydra.

111
00:08:32,670 --> 00:08:34,330
I've read an account of one before.

112
00:08:35,510 --> 00:08:39,210
An infernal dragon covered in magic stone scales that absorb mana.

113
00:08:39,970 --> 00:08:43,210
I thought it was a fairy tale, but it appears they do exist.

114
00:08:44,470 --> 00:08:45,250
Mana absorption.

115
00:08:46,230 --> 00:08:50,930
So, are you saying that you and I won't be able to damage that thing at all?

116
00:08:50,930 --> 00:08:56,510
Well, if the book I read was telling the truth, then magic might work if you fire point blank.

117
00:08:56,990 --> 00:09:00,370
Still gonna revive itself, so what are we supposed to do about that?

118
00:09:01,390 --> 00:09:02,750
That is a nuisance.

119
00:09:06,310 --> 00:09:10,090
I've heard that if you burn the stump where the head was cut off, it won't be able to regenerate.

120
00:09:10,090 --> 00:09:13,810
At least that's how Heracles did it in Greek mythology.

121
00:09:14,810 --> 00:09:19,730
He lopped off the Hydra's heads one by one and used a torch to cauterize the open wounds so it couldn't heal.

122
00:09:21,310 --> 00:09:24,570
Not that ancient folktales are a particularly credible source.

123
00:09:24,950 --> 00:09:25,750
That's a thought.

124
00:09:26,390 --> 00:09:27,690
Kill the tissue there.

125
00:09:27,950 --> 00:09:28,370
Yeah.

126
00:09:29,050 --> 00:09:32,810
We don't have torches, but it shouldn't be able to deflect magic where it doesn't have scales.

127
00:09:33,750 --> 00:09:34,070
Huh.

128
00:09:34,070 --> 00:09:35,490
I guess it's worth a shot.

129
00:09:36,410 --> 00:09:36,850
Okay.

130
00:09:37,330 --> 00:09:38,750
I'm all in if you guys are.

131
00:09:39,370 --> 00:09:40,110
What do you think?

132
00:09:40,250 --> 00:09:41,270
That work for you, Paul?

133
00:09:42,710 --> 00:09:43,190
Yeah.

134
00:09:43,810 --> 00:09:45,410
You don't sound too enthusiastic.

135
00:09:46,130 --> 00:09:47,030
Weren't you listening?

136
00:09:47,450 --> 00:09:50,410
You're the only one of us who can chop that thing's heads off.

137
00:09:51,810 --> 00:09:54,910
Paul severs the heads, I cauterize the wounds.

138
00:09:55,790 --> 00:09:58,870
And chances are, I'll have to do it at melee range.

139
00:09:58,870 --> 00:09:58,970
Huh.

140
00:10:04,070 --> 00:10:09,330
Alina Lys, Talhand, Geese, Roxy.

141
00:10:10,950 --> 00:10:12,590
You've done so much for me.

142
00:10:13,590 --> 00:10:16,590
You've traveled the world for me, for my family.

143
00:10:17,410 --> 00:10:19,770
Went to lengths I couldn't dream to ask of you.

144
00:10:20,710 --> 00:10:22,870
And this is where it all ends.

145
00:10:23,490 --> 00:10:24,910
We're going to save Zenith.

146
00:10:25,430 --> 00:10:29,530
But even if we can't, at least my family is accounted for.

147
00:10:30,990 --> 00:10:32,610
Please lend me your strength.

148
00:10:32,610 --> 00:10:35,010
This one last time.

149
00:10:35,690 --> 00:10:37,030
How could I say no?

150
00:10:37,230 --> 00:10:38,970
You're acting so humble for once.

151
00:10:39,210 --> 00:10:39,990
Heavens, Paul.

152
00:10:40,310 --> 00:10:42,490
What fool would say no after all of this?

153
00:10:43,130 --> 00:10:44,890
You know you can always count on me.

154
00:10:45,290 --> 00:10:45,910
I'm in.

155
00:10:46,250 --> 00:10:47,210
Let's win this.

156
00:10:47,650 --> 00:10:49,710
We've made it this far because we worked together.

157
00:10:50,190 --> 00:10:51,330
We can't turn back now.

158
00:10:51,330 --> 00:11:03,330
Rudy, my boy.

159
00:11:03,790 --> 00:11:05,630
I'm so lucky to have a son like you.

160
00:11:06,030 --> 00:11:06,950
Come on, Dad.

161
00:11:07,050 --> 00:11:07,490
Lighten up.

162
00:11:07,990 --> 00:11:09,730
You can flatter me after we beat the Hydra.

163
00:11:09,890 --> 00:11:10,790
It's not flattery.

164
00:11:11,190 --> 00:11:12,550
It's true, and I mean it.

165
00:11:12,550 --> 00:11:16,650
I can't keep a cool head like you.

166
00:11:16,730 --> 00:11:17,390
I never could.

167
00:11:18,470 --> 00:11:20,130
I don't come up with grand ideas.

168
00:11:20,410 --> 00:11:23,150
I'm just an idiot who charges in headfirst without thinking.

169
00:11:23,930 --> 00:11:25,190
I'm an awful dad.

170
00:11:25,190 --> 00:11:27,670
You deserve better, Rudy.

171
00:11:28,670 --> 00:11:29,730
I failed you.

172
00:11:32,330 --> 00:11:34,930
With that in mind, I'm going to say this to you.

173
00:11:35,850 --> 00:11:38,630
This is something a parent should never say to their child.

174
00:11:39,290 --> 00:11:39,470
Ready?

175
00:11:39,470 --> 00:11:40,470
Yes.

176
00:11:44,470 --> 00:11:46,470
Save your mother, even if it kills you.

177
00:11:47,830 --> 00:11:48,350
Sir!

178
00:11:51,030 --> 00:11:51,550
Okay.

179
00:11:52,050 --> 00:11:52,650
Let's go.

180
00:11:54,450 --> 00:11:55,270
He's right.

181
00:11:55,510 --> 00:11:56,790
No parent should say that.

182
00:11:57,230 --> 00:11:58,590
But he's not being cruel.

183
00:11:58,890 --> 00:11:59,970
He's showing his conviction.

184
00:12:00,650 --> 00:12:01,690
His trust in me.

185
00:12:02,490 --> 00:12:03,830
I have to honor it.

186
00:12:05,610 --> 00:12:07,310
We're going to save Zenith.

187
00:12:07,310 --> 00:12:11,310
To that end, Paul and I would share the same determination.

188
00:12:21,310 --> 00:12:21,750
Ready?

189
00:12:22,270 --> 00:12:22,930
Let's go!

190
00:12:37,310 --> 00:12:47,810
Yeah, looks like I'll have to get up close after all.

191
00:12:48,130 --> 00:12:49,250
Just as we predicted.

192
00:12:49,630 --> 00:12:50,710
So, can you do it?

193
00:12:50,970 --> 00:12:51,850
I think I can.

194
00:12:52,350 --> 00:12:52,610
Rudy!

195
00:12:53,210 --> 00:12:54,370
Stay right behind me.

196
00:12:54,470 --> 00:12:55,450
This thing is no joke.

197
00:12:55,810 --> 00:12:56,070
Right!

198
00:12:56,070 --> 00:13:10,730
Fight him up!

199
00:13:14,730 --> 00:13:15,610
Who's that?

200
00:13:15,610 --> 00:13:27,030
Yes!

201
00:13:27,030 --> 00:13:28,710
It works!

202
00:13:29,390 --> 00:13:30,030
Atta boy!

203
00:13:39,610 --> 00:13:40,570
Come for me!

204
00:13:40,570 --> 00:13:41,750
I've got you!

205
00:13:45,190 --> 00:13:45,870
Roxy!

206
00:13:47,610 --> 00:13:50,310
Let this divine power be rich and nourishing.

207
00:13:50,790 --> 00:13:51,130
Healing!

208
00:13:56,870 --> 00:13:58,010
Now, son!

209
00:13:58,330 --> 00:13:58,790
Audit!

210
00:14:04,570 --> 00:14:04,990
Move!

211
00:14:04,990 --> 00:14:06,030
It's coming our way!

212
00:14:06,030 --> 00:14:28,910
Let this divine power be rich and nourishing.

213
00:14:28,910 --> 00:14:29,650
Healing!

214
00:14:29,650 --> 00:14:31,910
Many thanks.

215
00:14:31,910 --> 00:14:39,230
Now's our chance.

216
00:14:39,490 --> 00:14:40,250
Let's go, Rudy!

217
00:14:41,830 --> 00:14:42,350
Wait.

218
00:14:43,130 --> 00:14:44,130
Something's not right.

219
00:14:47,090 --> 00:14:47,610
What?

220
00:14:51,210 --> 00:14:51,730
No!

221
00:14:51,830 --> 00:14:53,190
Don't give that thing time to heal!

222
00:14:53,330 --> 00:14:54,230
Get in there now!

223
00:14:54,230 --> 00:15:00,570
Let the great protection of ice crail me at the place thou seekest.

224
00:15:00,730 --> 00:15:03,030
Call forth your glacial torrent here and now!

225
00:15:03,470 --> 00:15:04,470
Ice smash!

226
00:15:05,730 --> 00:15:06,090
